{
  "title": "Title-case section labels survive ingredient parsing",
  "description": "The Smitten Kitchen pancetta white bean pot pie ingredient \
fixture still emits `Lid` and `Filling` as ingredients because the source \
labels are title-case lines without colons. Existing section-header detection \
handles colon-suffixed labels and all-caps labels, but not these short \
title-case labels. Investigate a narrow section-label heuristic that filters \
this fixture without dropping real one-word ingredients.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 4,
